<title>NETHERLANDS: Aegon sets 1996 stock div at one for 93.</title>
<headline>Aegon sets 1996 stock div at one for 93.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Insurer Aegon NV said on Tuesday it had set the stock alternative to its 1996 final dividend at one new share for every 93 shares already held.</p>
<p>In March, Aegon announced it would pay a 1993 cash dividend of 2.79 guilders, of which 1.18 guilders had already been paid as an interim dividend. It said at the time that the final payment could be taken up in cash or in new shares.</p>
<p>Aegon shares closed at 142.80 guilders on the Amsterdam Stock Exchange on Tuesday, down 2.40 from their previous close.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000 (fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
